":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","color":"447744","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-05-23T15:31:49Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T17:24:37Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6119) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Select Points mode in Path3D and Path2D's curve editor, CTRL+left click will add a new point. However, this conflict with the Modo 3D navigation mode where CTRL+ALT+left click is used to rotate the view.\n\nThe solution would be to check that only CTRL is pressed when adding a new point (e.g. ALT is NOT pressed).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1) Go to `Editor >  Editor Settings > Editors > 3D > Navigation Scheme` and change it to Modo\n2) Create a Path2D or 3D\n3) Try to rotate the view with ALT+CTRL+left click\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo need.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106753/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}